.TH TULPAR-REPO 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.6.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-repo \- manage configured repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar repo add
.I url
.RI [ \-\-user ]
.br
.B tulpar repo remove
.I url
.RI [ \-\-user ]
.br
.B tulpar repo enable
.I url
.RI [ \-\-user ]
.br
.B tulpar repo disable
.I url
.RI [ \-\-user ]
.br
.B tulpar repo priority
.I url number
.RI [ \-\-user ]
.br
.B tulpar repo list
.RI [ \-\-all ]
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B tulpar repo update
.br
.B tulpar e
.I action
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B tulpar \-e
.I action
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manages the list of configured Tulpar Server repositories.
.TP
.B add
Appends a repository URL to the repository list file.
.TP
.B remove
Removes a repository URL from the repository list file.
.TP
.B enable
Re-enables a repository that was disabled.
.TP
.B disable
Keeps a repository in the list but stops using it. The entry is stored
as a
.B #disabled
comment line, which older versions ignore.
.TP
.B priority
Sets the priority of a repository. Repositories are consulted in
ascending order of priority, ties keep their order in the files; the
default is 100. The value is stored as a
.B priority=N
word after the URL.
.TP
.B list
Prints every enabled repository in consultation order, system-wide and
per-user combined.
.B \-\-all
adds disabled repositories and prints the state, URL and priority
separated by tabs.
.B \-\-json
prints the same information as JSON; see
.BR tulpar-json (7).
.TP
.B update
Refreshes the cached
.B repodata.json
for every configured repository, ignoring the cache TTL.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-user
For
.BR add ,
.BR remove ,
.BR enable ,
.B disable
and
.BR priority ,
operate on the per-user repository list
.RI ( "~/.config/apg/repos" )
instead of the system-wide one
.RI ( "/etc/apg/repos" ).
When omitted,
.B add
uses the system-wide file if tulpar is running as root and the
per-user file otherwise; the other actions edit the file that already
contains the repository. Editing keeps comments and unrelated lines
intact.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apg/repos
System-wide repository list, one URL per line, optionally followed by
.BR priority=N .
Lines starting with
.B #
are comments, except
.B #disabled
followed by an entry, which marks that entry as disabled.
.TP
.I ~/.config/apg/repos
Per-user repository list, same format.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if the requested repository could not be
added, removed, or refreshed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-search (1)
